---
interface Props {
  minWeek: number | null;
  firstNum: number;
  lastNum: number;
  firstDate: string;
  lastDate: string;
  beforeWindow: number;
  nonAttack: number;
  aria: string;
}
const { minWeek, firstNum, lastNum, firstDate, lastDate, beforeWindow, nonAttack, aria } = Astro.props as Props;
const heading = minWeek !== null && minWeek > 0
  ? "Shipping attacks have continued every week since July"
  : "How often shipping attacks are reported";
const weeklyClaim = minWeek !== null && minWeek > 0
  ? `UKMTO recorded at least ${minWeek === 1 ? "one attack report" : `${minWeek} attack reports`} in each complete week shown.`
  : "The chart counts attack reports by week, including weeks with none recorded.";
---

<div class="mt-12 mb-3">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">{heading}</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
    The UK Maritime Trade Operations centre (UKMTO), run by the Royal Navy, collects reports from merchant ships
    in the Gulf, the Red Sea, and the Gulf of Aden. {weeklyClaim} Oil can keep moving through these routes while
    ships are still being attacked.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
    These are reported attacks, not a count of every attack. UKMTO says some strikes probably go unreported.
    Hijackings, advisories, and suspicious activity are recorded separately and aren't included here.
  </p>
</div>
<div class="h-64 sm:h-72">
  <canvas id="ukmtoChart" role="img" aria-label={aria}></canvas>
</div>
<p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-ink/60 sm:text-xs tabular">
  Source: <a href="https://www.ukmto.org/recent-incidents" class="underline">UKMTO attack reports</a>, {firstDate}–{lastDate}, 2026. Weeks run Monday–Sunday, by incident date. Lighter bars mark
  partial weeks; the latest week is still in progress.
</p>
<details class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink/60">
  <summary class="cursor-pointer">How the reports are counted</summary>
  <p class="mt-2">
    This chart uses reports #{firstNum} through #{lastNum}, as of {lastDate}, 2026.
    UKMTO numbers reports for the year; {beforeWindow} came before this chart's start, including three before
    the war began on February 28. We keep earlier entries as UKMTO's recent-incidents page moves forward.
    The {nonAttack} reports classified as hijackings, advisories, or suspicious activity aren't counted as attacks.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Reports #99, #100, and #125 are missing from the captured page. The Joint Maritime Information Center's
    August 4 update records Egyptian authorities identifying #99 and #100 as likely drone attacks.
    Those two reports aren't included in the bars, and #125 remains unaccounted for. Other unreported attacks
    may also be missing.
  </p>
</details>
